      "content": "The arguments that UBI is too expensive or will destroy work incentives are often based on outdated economic models that ignore the reality of a hyper-competitive, AI-driven labor market where traditional jobs are vanishing. Proponents of UBI frequently cite the \"work disincentive\" myth, yet data from pilot programs in Finland and Kenya shows that people actually work *more* when they have financial security, proving that basic needs don't drive productivity. While the cost is high, the alternative of letting millions fall into poverty while tech monopolies profit is a far more expensive societal failure that no responsible government should accept.",
      "source": "target",
